Interestingly, I reported this a few days ago and it has disappeared.

The basic problem is that ks.test() returns the p-value "< 2.2e-16" and 
RPy converts this in -2.2e-16 sometimes, and sometimes to 0.0.  It's 
hrd to say what it should return, but returning a negative value is 
certainly incorrect.  Probably +2.2e-16 would be the best choice.

This was using RPy version 0.4.6 and R version 2.2.1.

